    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, our offensive core is anchored by the dual-threat upside of **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (76.97) and **Bryce Harper** (76.31). **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** benefits significantly from a favorable matchup against Murphy, where wind-out conditions at the park provide a tangible ceiling boost to his already elite projection. Similarly, **Bryce Harper** stands out as an essential start; despite the platoon disadvantage against Kent, his high-end xwOBA of .389 and the favorable SP skill matchup (5.54 xERA) keep him well within our elite tier. While **Cal Raleigh** (68.23) projects slightly lower, his power potential against the soft-tossing Johnson remains our most reliable high-leverage opportunity for HR and RBI production.\n\nPlatoon edges are dictating the back end of our roster, with **Jung Hoo Lee** (60.52) and **Daulton Varsho** (60.09) both earning strong start grades. **Jung Hoo Lee** is particularly interesting today; beyond his platoon advantage, the matchup includes a favorable factor for his speed profile\u2014the opposing pitcher\u2019s slow delivery allows for a 2% boost to his SB probability, a vital consideration given our emphasis on stolen bases. Conversely, **Jeremiah Jackson** (45.76) remains our most vulnerable starter. His projection is stunted by a matchup against the elite Manaea and the high risk of a \"hold\" situation, though he stays in the lineup due to the scarcity of high-speed alternatives.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Gleyber Torres** (50.44), who fell just shy of replacing the struggling **Jeremiah Jackson**. While **Gleyber Torres** carries a solid 8% bump from his #2 batting spot, the negative dynamic platoon adjustment against Fisher dragged his overall efficiency below our threshold for starting him over our optimized outfield configuration. We are also closely monitoring the status of our middle-to-bottom tier options like **Alex Freeland** (55.39) and **Masyn Winn** (54.79); both are currently operating on thin margins, and while their matchups against Tidwell and Lowder are soft enough to warrant inclusion, they are the first candidates for removal should we need to protect our remaining game caps later in the week.",
